w: 1.~Lamp of our feet! where- by we trace Our path, when wont to stray;
w: 2.~Bread of our souls! where- on we feed; True man- na from on high!
w: 3.~Pil- lar of fire\- through watch- es dark! Or ra- diant cloud by day!
w: 4.~Pole\- star on life's tem- pest- uous deep! Bea- con! when doubts sur- round;
w: 5.~Rich- es in pov- er- ty! our aid In ev- ery need- ful hour!
w: 6.~Our shield and buck- ler in the fight! Vic- t'ry's tri- um- phant palm!
w: 7.~Child- hood's pre- cep- tor! man- hood's trust! Old a- ge's firm al- ly!
w: 8.~Pure o- ra- cles of truth di- vine! Un- like each fa- bled dream
w: 9.~Word of the e- ver\-- li- ving God! Will of His glor- ious Son!
w: 10.~Yet to un- fold thy hid- den worth, Thy my- ste- ries to reveal,
w: 11.~And we, if we a- right would learn The wis- dom it im- parts,
